PROJECT STRUCTURE:-

mira-hotel-agent/
│
├── agent/
│   ├── agent.py          # Conversation orchestration
│   ├── llm.py            # Intent extraction & responses
│   ├── state.py          # Persistent guest state
│   ├── tools.py          # Hotel search & hotel tools
│   └── recommendation.py # Hotel ranking logic(incomplete)
│
├── data/
│   └── hotels.json       # Hotel & room inventory
│
├── tests/                # Test cases
│
├── app.py                # Streamlit UI
├── test_conversation.py  # End-to-end conversation test
├── requirements.txt
├── .env                  # API key (not committed)
└── README.md

Component Responsibilities
app.py:- Streamlit chat interface and UI
agent.py:-	Conversation orchestration and booking flow
llm.py:-	Natural-language intent extraction
state.py:-	Maintains guest and booking state
tools.py:-	Deterministic hotel/property search
hotels.json:-	Structured hotel and room inventory
tests/:-	Test cases and validation

Design Principle

LLM handles understanding and conversation.
Deterministic Python logic handles hotel data, filtering, validation and booking state.

This separation reduces the risk of hallucinating hotel names, prices or room information.

Environment Variables

Mira currently requires the following environment variable:-
GEMINI_API_KEY,	Google Gemini API key used for natural-language intent extraction	

Assumptions-
Hotel and room information is stored in a structured local JSON inventory.
Hotel prices represent the price per night.
The guest's budget is interpreted as the maximum acceptable nightly room price.
Room capacity must be sufficient for the requested number of guests.
The current booking flow assumes one room unless the guest specifies otherwise.
Dates are interpreted using the current year when the year is not explicitly provided.
Booking confirmation represents a simulated booking flow; it does not connect to a real hotel reservation system.
Hotel availability is based on the provided inventory rather than a live hotel booking API.

CONVERSATIONAL FLOW:-

Guest Request
      ↓
Extract Requirements
      ↓
Update Guest State
      ↓
Missing Information?
   ↙          ↘
 YES           NO
  ↓             ↓
Ask Guest    Search Hotels
                ↓
         Select Hotel
                ↓
          Select Room
                ↓
        Collect Dates
                ↓
        Confirm Booking


CORE COMPONENTS:-

MiraAgent
Controls the conversation and booking state transitions.

GuestState
Maintains destination, guests, budget, preferences, selected hotel/room, dates and booking status across messages.

Tools
Perform deterministic operations against the hotel inventory instead of allowing the LLM to invent hotel information.

Hotel Inventory
A structured JSON dataset containing fictional properties, rooms, prices, capacities and amenities.

Streamlit UI
Provides the conversational interface and displays the current booking state.

Key Features:-
Natural-language requirement extraction
Persistent conversation state
Deterministic hotel search
Hotel and room selection
Budget and capacity filtering
Date validation
No-result handling
Booking confirmation flow
Streamlit chat interface


Tech Stack:-

Python
Google Gemini API
Streamlit
JSON
Dataclasses
python-dotenv

Known Limitations:-
The hotel inventory is static and stored locally in hotels.json.
There is no live connection to hotel booking or availability systems.
The current system does not process real payments.
Booking confirmation is simulated and does not create a real reservation.
The system currently supports a limited set of properties and room types.
Natural-language date extraction depends on the supported intent-extraction logic.
The system does not currently maintain bookings in a persistent database.
Multi-room and complex group-booking scenarios have limited support.
Hotel recommendations are based on the available inventory and deterministic matching/ranking rather than real-time market data.

